 snow that is generally all faceted. When we get some snow slopes like this will have a connected weak layer. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Fore- and mid ground slopes are snow free. The alpine slopes in the distance have a shallow coating of snow.","dateTaken":"2026-11-15T22:38:36.884Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"57346306-9e5a-5d41-a7f0-2ce0015d1f44","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1793997784/AvIDfx/icjusqdprrk0hpzhydys.webp","width":2500,"height":1407,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eMt. Richthofen and Mt. Mahler above Lake Agnes, near Cameron Pass. The slopes in these photos are mainly northwest-, north-, and northeast-facing.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Steep, alpine peaks with a thin coating of snow.","dateTaken":"2026-11-05T20:47:16.593Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"fa87ef37-4726-537c-bf5c-9bcb34f46e87","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794861415/AvIDfx/urzpzqb7izkjatjuzlya.webp","width":1202,"height":1602,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eSurfaces in the Northern Mountains are generally very weak but there is no slab to cause an avalanche problem currently. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Large feather like surface hoar.","dateTaken":"2026-11-15T16:57:21Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"e5ed8e17-a921-5d03-b26d-c7c89bdc8a0e","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794861489/AvIDfx/ksh7ritug6tb8wxzfmg3.webp","width":2500,"height":1406,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis footage from Coffee Pot road in the Flat Tops shows that although they may look snowy from a distance the coverage is pretty patchy \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A cliff-topped ridge with snowy slopes in the background transitions to forests and then ranches.","dateTaken":"2026-11-14T20:57:53.699Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-18T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-19T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}},{"id":"f00c2898-0266-4a9e-b47e-8c15bce99899","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["028E2912-5D1A-4EC6-A22D-2180A797ECDD","071639C0-9D38-49C1-8AF3-F227A80F447D","3194EF47-46C9-4132-83C1-D156F9B94123","383548A5-2C8E-4CC6-985E-83F7AE17EAB6","7BA4F5A7-6E11-4A81-88FC-0A72429699A0","97694259-0F92-4CE6-A4C9-3A69D2C33F35","9DFB3103-D688-4AB3-B16D-EE6A20EA25A7","DAFC9825-B67E-4FF5-8E6C-4D05CC20E554"],"areaId":"eca6af8f59fdab95df2c9f6c913105e1d0407b0e9e2529069d4c3cc896761eae","issueDateTime":"2026-11-17T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-18T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-18T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eStrong winds will drift the little bit of new snow, making it easy to trigger a small avalanche below ridgelines. Look for stiffer snow below cornices, and steer around steep slopes where you encounter hollow-feeling drifts or experience cracking in the snow surface. Choose wind-sheltered slopes for a safer option.\u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"819c09a2-9022-5085-a7d5-9c0cddc46e50","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794861822/AvIDfx/sjyfyryy136v1hbfldwr.webp","width":2500,"height":1681,"credit":"CBAC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis recent avalanche is the largest reported in days and it shows what's in store when a new slab forms. A weak, continuous layer of facets is now buried throughout most W-N-E-facing terrain at higher elevations, and it just needs a slab on top to become dangerous.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A fresh avalanche in steep, rocky terrain with a person standing at the toe of the debris","dateTaken":"2026-11-15T20:43:47.407Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"93973d38-4e6b-513d-934a-33178e0603aa","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794775466/AvIDfx/nxygtth6iycbqwalet1j.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"CAIC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThe highlighted ridgeline is a feature you should consider avoiding. A little new snow and gusty winds could form small surface slabs that could break loose and sweep you down onto the exposed rocks below.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A red circle highligts a snowy ridgeline","dateTaken":"2026-11-10T19:22:00Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"fe22735e-aa52-5939-b615-acb143276578","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794775711/AvIDfx/bgnndew1sgiwdgyxm9nn.webp","width":960,"height":540,"credit":"CAIC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThe snowpack is very weak at the surface with a supportive crust below. This setup will be dangerous once a new slab forms on top. Be on the lookout for any new drifted slabs at higher elevations, as they could be easy to trigger. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A snow pit with red arrow showing where it was recorded","dateTaken":"2026-11-10T20:48:40.268Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"db2b9c04-c40d-5f96-af55-f52ae98302d9","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794688718/AvIDfx/hqq7lyxsaxsx7dfqdw4i.webp","width":350,"height":263,"credit":"CBAC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThese small-grain facets are widespread across W-N-E-facing terrain and will become a problematic layer once a slab forms on top of them. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A crystal card with small grained facets","dateTaken":"2026-11-12T20:38:47.333Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"moderate","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-18T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"moderate","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-19T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[{"type":"windSlab","aspectElevations":["nw_alp","n_alp","ne_alp","e_alp","w_alp"],"likelihood":"likely","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"1.5"}}],[{"type":"windSlab","aspectElevations":["nw_alp","n_alp","ne_alp","e_alp","w_alp"],"likelihood":"likely","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"1.5"}}]]}},{"id":"a8760abc-0e2e-4350-869a-e82609d3fea6","type":"avalancheforeca